ewCommandTimeout value from driver.capabilities in the session-creation cell result. This is the Appium idle-command timeout, not the python_exec timeout or the task business/cleanup deadline; all existing task budgets and cleanup requirements remain unchanged.\n\nSession startup can exceed the default 30-second execution deadline. In the python_exec request that creates the session, explicitly set timeout=90; create the driver and capture its session ID in that cell before UI actions. The isolated MCP transport deadline is 120000 milliseconds, distinct from the active-cell timeout. Neither setting increases the task step limit or total Agent timeout. Do not retry session creation after an uncertain result: reconcile the owned session instead.\n\nFinish with a dedicated python_exec cleanup cell: retain the owned session ID, call driver.quit(), and make the cell's final expression exactly {\"ownedSessionId\": session_id, \"quitReturned\": True} only after quit returns. If quit fails, let the cell fail; never claim cleanup from a local variable or prose. Return one compact JSON object with taskOutcome, sessionCleanup, and evidence, but do not repeat the session ID in that final response. A textual success claim is not the verdict; AndroidWorld evaluates device state independently, and only the observed cleanup cell proves session cleanup.",
